Bookings:
*Updated 2026-10-12 to match the Harbor design (design/harbor/client/static/book-*.html). The design is the source of truth.*

Only families with an approved skater can book. A family still waiting sees "Booking opens once Coach <name> approves"
instead (ADR-022 d6). *With several coaches it names each one: "Booking opens once Coach Dana or Coach Ben approves"
(2026-10-13, ADR-025 i).*

Booking for: at the top of every booking page. With one approved skater it names them; with more, a switch picks which
skater is being booked. Changing skater clears the picked times.

The booking PAGE view will only show the next 3 months. ~~This is a UI restriction only. nothing validates against it api/server level~~ Example: its April 24th, so the months shown would be April, May, June.
*Changed 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decision 3): the system now checks the 3-month window too, not just the page.*
  Each picked time must be inside the months the page shows, in the coach's time zone.
  A repeating booking is checked on its first date only. Its later dates can run past the window, up to the end date.
  A pick outside the window refuses the whole request: "That date is further ahead than you can book." Nothing is
    booked. (The page never offers such a date, so this only happens from outside the booking page.)
  Resubmitting the same request just after a new month starts isn't refused: it gets the same result as the first time.
The Booking Page will show a calendar view with the months available on the right hand side. Clicking each month will show the availability for that month. Availability is shown by having each square (whichrepresenting a day within that month) with the number of open lesson slots. A day that has no open lessons slots is ~~dark grey/~~disabled and cannot be clicked. On the left hand side next to the calendar view is ~~week 1-4~~ *one week link per row of the calendar ("Week 1", "Week 2", ...), with its dates; a week with nothing open says "Nothing open" and can't be clicked*. Clicking on a week link takes the client to that weekds Schedule view. Clicking on a day within the calendar takes you to that day's Schedule view.
*Design additions:*
  Each month on the right shows how many open times it has. Previous and next arrows move between the three months.
  A day where the skater already has a lesson is marked with a tick and their first name.
  A time-off day says "No lessons".
  A "Booking window" note: you can see three months ahead; a repeating booking can run past that.
  Coach hasn't posted any times: the calendar is greyed out with "No lesson times yet" ~~and an
    "Email me when times appear" button~~. *Removed 2026-10-13: no email when times appear.*

A schedule view will ~~have time blocks starting at the coaches first lesson of the day, and going until the last lesson of the day, The Interval btwn the start of day and end of day will be the length of lessons. Example, Coaches first lesson of the day is 6am and the lesson is 30 mins, then the schedule will display the times 6:00 -6:30 6:30-7:00 etc up to the end of the day.~~ The schedule view will display the results from the coachs schedule query.
*Design:* the day's times as a timeline, grouped by the coach's blocks. Each block is labelled with its name, lesson
  length and price, and its times run from its start to its end at that length. A gap between blocks shows
  "Not on the ice <from> – <to>". Longer lessons are drawn taller.
  Each time shows its start and end, length, and price. A taken time says only "Taken" (who holds it is never shown).
  The family's own lessons are shown by the skater's name. Times already passed say "Past". *2026-10-13 (owner): every time that has already started says "Past",
  booked or not, including the family's own lesson and other families' bookings.*
  A day strip across the top shows the week, with each day's open count ("No ice" or "Full" when there's nothing),
  and arrows to the previous and next week. Picks are kept while moving between days.
  A special schedule day shows a banner with its name and dates. A time-off day says the coach is away.


A client will book by clicking on one or more open time block slot and hitting ~~submit~~ *Continue*. Clicking the block will select/deselect the lesson.
~~Each selected slot will be highlighted light green while the unselected are white with grey border and the already taken time slots are a medium grey.~~
*Design:* open, "Your pick", taken and "Your family's lesson" each have their own look, explained in a legend under the
  timeline. Colors follow the Harbor theme.
*Design:* a "Your picks" panel beside the timeline lists every picked time (any day) with its price and an X to remove
  it, the total time and total price, and the Continue button.
After selecting the slot(s) they want want they will hit ~~submit~~ *Continue*. A pop up will display the selected slot(s) and have a reoccuring checkbox ("Repeat these lessons") next to it, a disabled frequency dropdown, and a disabled endDate date field. If the checkbox is selected then the dropdown is enabled and shows ~~1 week, 2 week, 3 week, or 4 week~~ *Every week, Every 2 weeks, Every 3 weeks, Every 4 weeks*. defaulted to 1 week.  The endDate ("Until") date field is enabled and defaults to 3 months from ~~that date~~ *the first picked date*.
*Design additions to the pop-up:*
  A repeating booking can run up to 12 months. An end date before the first lesson, or more than 12 months out, shows an error.
  Every picked time repeats on the same day of the week.
  A summary: how many lessons in all (and until when), the first week's total, and the total for all lessons.
  Note: you pay the coach directly; BladeBook only sends reminders.
  Buttons: Back, and "Book N lessons" (the total count).

A confirmation page will display afterwards showing the successful and unsuccessful bookings. If any bookings are unsuccessful list the unsuccessful dates ~~and ask the client to retry~~.
*Design:*
  A headline: how many lessons were booked for the skater, and that a confirmation email is on its way.
  One card per picked time (or repeating series) with a bar showing how many dates were booked, already theirs, or unavailable.
  Each date that couldn't be booked is listed with the reason (e.g. another family took it, time off, no times of that
  length that week) and a "Pick another time" button. The family can also leave them; the rest are confirmed.
  Resubmitting: a time already booked for this skater is recognised and never booked twice (ADR-006 d4b). Those dates
  are listed as "Already booked". If an earlier attempt booked a series that isn't in the new request, the page asks
  whether to keep or cancel it.
  Buttons: "Book more" and "View my bookings".

At least one lesson slot must be selected for the ~~Submit~~ *Continue* button to enabled. If the reocurring checkbox is unselected then the reoccuring frequency dropdown value in the object being submitted is set to null/empty.



*More than one coach (decided by the owner 2026-10-13; ADR-025; book-times-coach-switch.html,
book-confirm-two-coaches.html, book-result-two-coaches.html, book-result-coach-failed.html):*
  A "Coach" dropdown sits next to "Booking for". It lists the coaches the selected skater is with; a coach
    still to approve that skater is listed but can't be picked. The pages show one coach's times at a time.
  Switching coach keeps the times picked with other coaches (a note says so). Switching skater clears all picks.
  "Your picks" groups picks by coach, with a total per coach and no total across coaches.
  Both booking pages show the selected coach's cancellation notice period.
  A time that overlaps the skater's lesson or pick with another coach is marked, not blocked. Only overlapping
    times clash; lessons that only touch don't. Travel time between rinks is Phase 3.
  Confirm pop-up: picks listed per coach, a lesson count and total per coach, every clashing date listed and the
    button reads "Book anyway". One Repeat and Until apply to every pick. With more than one coach it says
    "Coaches can have different cancellation notice periods."
  Result: one section per coach. Each coach's booking goes through on its own; if one fails, its section says
    nothing was booked with that coach and offers "Try again", which resends only that coach's picks and never
    books anything twice.
  Clashes are only warned about to the family; the coach isn't told.

Lessons can be split: reference 'Schedule lesson split' for details
*Design (book-share-confirm.html, book-share-no-match.html, book-share-result.html): the box is in the confirm pop-up, only when a picked time can be shared.*
*Added 2026-10-13 (ADR-031 decisions 5 and 10):* the invited skater's place is held as soon as the family books, so no
  one else can take it. The booking family pays the full price until the invited skater joins. One invitation covers
  every date of a repeating booking. Sharing is offered only here, while booking, and on a freed place in My bookings
  (see 'Schedule lesson split').
*Changed 2026-10-20 (ADR-033 d2, d2a):* only a skater the coach has accepted can be invited. As soon as the share code
  is entered, the booking page checks it with the share-check endpoint. If the skater isn't the coach's student, the
  share step stops with: "Mia R. isn't one of Coach Dana's students yet. Mia's family can sign up with Coach Dana's
  code, and once Coach Dana accepts Mia you can share a lesson." Nothing is booked.
  Book stays off while the share-code box has anything in it, until the check passes. If the check fails or is rate-limited: "Couldn't check that code. Try again." Changing the code checks again; clearing it books a private lesson. (ADR-033 2a, 2026-10-20)
  A sibling the coach hasn't accepted yet shows as "not available to add until Coach Dana accepts them" and can't be
  picked.
